ously place the race in the Republican column, most calling it Solid or Safe Republican.\n\nTwo Democratic-sponsored polls show a much closer contest, with Letlow ahead by about four points, and a favorable national environment for Democrats narrows the underlying gap. Even so, prediction markets give Davis only a four to nine percent chance of winning. The weight of the evidence points to a Likely Republican hold, with genuine but limited uncertainty from thin, partisan-sponsored polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0575, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0895, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0752, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0962, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1593, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0984, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1142, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0801, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0698, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0644, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0666, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0772, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0599, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.1108, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.0727, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.0549, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.0401, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.0649, "margin": -9.0}]}